    crm:P129i_is_subject_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/diary/1908/document/206> ;
    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493338149/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """wretched boys had to puzzle over his story, and old fogeys said he was mythical, whatever that might be. Yes, he was dead and gone, with the horses he had tamed; it wasn’t any use bothering about him. He must have been a nice chap though, for they made such a fuss over his death, his father rolling in the mud and all!
Sometimes he murmured to himself, “Alfred, tamer of horses”, but it didn’t go so well as Hector.
And no one could understand why the boy tried so often, that summer, to teach his pony tricks. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 206 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1908> .

